Architecture (ADR-002/004/005/006/011):
  The web page owns no API data source — it renders from local state and wraps the already-ported NotificationSettings
  surface (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/NotificationSettings*.cs, its own parity unit with its own state
  matrix). This page therefore composes the shared PageContainer surface (the parity port of
  web/src/components/layout/PageContainer.tsx) for the title + muted subtitle + "Copy link" affordance, and hosts the
  NotificationSettings surface as PageContent. The shell-default NotificationSettings is wired over
  EmptyNotificationTabSignalsSource + the in-memory permission/push/sound stores (the EmptyXSource convention used by
  every sibling default port), so the settings surface renders the empty data state (web on-by-default toggles).

Data sources (manifest: none — renders from navigation params / local state):
  (none at the page tier) — no SSE/live data, so no staleness chip (ADR-013 n/a). The embedded NotificationSettings owns
  its loading / empty / error / stale / offline matrix; the page-tier PageContainer is shown with content (no page-level
  loading/empty/error props, exactly as the web page passes none).
Units (P1/S5): none rendered at this tier (no SI quantities on the page chrome).

